+## 7. Structured review delivery (mode: code_review)
+
+### 7.1 Validate the Analyzer handoff in PLANNING
+
+Resolve `{plugin_root}` to the absolute installed coding-agent plugin directory
+from the active plugin metadata or explicit task input; do not assume the
+current working directory is the plugin checkout. Read
+`{plugin_root}/skills/structured-review/SKILL.md` and the ticket state. The
+review_only route is ANALYSIS -> PLANNING -> COMPLETION. The Analyzer owns
+ANALYSIS; do not repeat it or jump directly to a terminal. Require the same
+`ticket_id`, `ticket_type=code_review`, retained function identity and the exact
+`states.ANALYSIS.deep_review_sha256` already bound to `deep-review.json`.
+
+Reuse these five artifacts from the Analyzer:
+- `deep-review-evidence.json`: actual rule_candidates and review_function request/results;
+- `deep-review.json`: typed structured partial review;
+- `review-report.md`: exact Markdown generated from that typed review;
+- `sequence.mmd` and `modules.mmd`: exact source-bound generated diagrams.
+
+Run `python3 "{plugin_root}/scripts/deep_review.py" verify --workspace "{workspace_dir}"` before
+accepting the handoff. Record the actual CLI result and error. Missing,
+unavailable, unsupported, truncated, stale, foreign or tampered inputs cannot be
+replaced with an empty/safe report. A partial result is usable only under the
+existing verifier conditions and with its limitations preserved. A denied
+transition or failed verification stays unresolved; do not mark delivery done.
+
+When additional factual evidence is required, the explicit aliases are
+`mcp__plugin_coding-agent_cks__cks_context_review_function` and
+`mcp__plugin_coding-agent_cks__cks_context_rule_candidates`. If unavailable,
+record the actual failed attempt. Select the exact retained function, explicit
+`go-local-review@1.0.0` pack and supported commit/source/snapshot pins; keep real
+requests/results and reuse the rule result's value/control view. Do not compute
+another graph or quietly substitute a different function or snapshot.
+
+### 7.2 Preserve typed scope and revise through ANALYSIS
+
+Preserve all six reasoning sections: data_state, guards_exceptions, complexity,
+resources, io, priority_tradeoffs; original-node evidence, assumptions/unknowns,
+computed/agent origins and `review_candidate` findings. Use priority
+`high | medium | low`, at most 32 findings. Do not introduce a critical severity
+or map another severity vocabulary silently. Section presence, one criterion,
+empty findings or changing a valid priority do not establish required-item
+completeness, priority correctness, safety or independent quality acceptance.
+
+The structural review stays `identity_only_unverified_snapshot`: matching
+identity is not an atomic snapshot or authenticated transport. The CFG is not
+a runtime trace; the module diagram is retained-file membership, with
+interprocedural relationships unknown. Byte equality is not rendering or
+semantic quality. Local receipt hashes do not authenticate reviewers.
+
+If the existing artifacts validate, reuse them on re-entry. Do not hand-edit
+Markdown, diagrams or computed data. If a reasoning/criteria revision is needed,
+return to ANALYSIS using the state-machine contract and hand the change back to
+the Analyzer. It rebuilds all five artifacts with `deep_review.py build`,
+revalidates and binds a new ANALYSIS hash. Clear the prior completed PLANNING
+report binding; do not reuse a stale report hash or rebind frozen identity in
+PLANNING. Then validate the new handoff here.
+
+### 7.3 Bind PLANNING and hand back to Orchestrator
+
+After successful validation, bind the exact bytes of `review-report.md` to
+`states.PLANNING.review_report_sha256`, set PLANNING.status=completed and keep
+current_state=PLANNING for the Orchestrator. Before terminal delivery, require
+the completion-state hook check and the same CLI verification of the recorded
+completion state: both the ANALYSIS and completed PLANNING bindings must match.
+The Orchestrator owns COMPLETION and must not report delivery before that check.
+
+The registered deep-review hook checks identified Write/Edit state changes;
+direct shell state edits are outside that hook and require the same CLI before
+delivery. Do not treat Bash as an automatic hook or permission bypass proof.
+Do not overwrite the validated report with the old free-form Markdown template.
+Report `validated_delivery` / `structured_partial_review` with independent
+acceptance `not_recorded`. No fix plan, production change, publication or tracker
+message is implied by this review delivery.
 
